            {
              "description": "The side menu with the panels. ## Files Import: a `.csv` file becomes a new data set that is selected (a header row names the columns, the last column is the label; labels 0 to k-1 make a classification data set, others a regression data set) and a `.json` config file replaces the network and data sets. Export: `text/csv` writes the active data set (class descriptions are not part of CSV); `application/json` writes the config and, once trained, the weights and biases of each layer under `weights`. The import of a `.json` file reads the config only and ignores `weights`, so a trained model is not restored. ## Signals - `history`: table of the training history, columns `epoch`, `loss`, `val_loss`, `acc`, `val_acc` (only the logged ones), one row per epoch. Empty before training. - `loss`: number, the training loss of the last epoch, or null before training. The widget has no effects: nothing from another widget fits a network.",
              "name": "menu"
            }
